<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul naphtha end-users suspend trade with Itochu.</title>
<headline>Seoul naphtha end-users suspend trade with Itochu.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean end-users of naphtha have temporarily suspended purchase from Itochu Corp accusing the Japanese firm of manipulating prices, an official at Daelim Corp said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;South Korean firms met today and decided to suspend naphtha purchase for three months beginning in December because of price manipulation by Itochu,&quot; said a Daelim official, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>He said South Korean naphtha end-users, including Daelim and Hyundai Petrochemical, agreed that current naphtha prices have been overvalued and manipulated by Japanese trader, Itochu Corp.</p>
<p>Naphtha purchase from Itochu would be suspended for February-April arrival, he said.</p>
</text>
